---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import { live, authors } from "../lib/rank.js";

const posts = (await getCollection("posts")).map((e) => e.data);
const shown = live(posts);
---

<Base title="About" description="How Intracloud works." path="/about">
  <h1>About Intracloud</h1>
  <p>
    Intracloud is a blog network with no signup, no forms, and no server. It
    indexes every file named <code>intracloud.md</code> on public GitHub whose
    frontmatter contains <code>intracloud: 1</code>, and renders them as a
    unified, prerendered feed.
  </p>
  <h2>Publish a post</h2>
  <p>Commit a file named <code>intracloud.md</code> anywhere in a public repo:</p>
  <pre><code>---
intracloud: 1
title: How I broke prod
tags: [postmortem]
---

Your markdown here.</code></pre>
  <p>
    A scheduled job discovers it (within the hour), rehosts its images, and
    publishes it. Your identity, avatar, and bio come from GitHub. Your publish
    date is when Intracloud first sees the file — it can't be gamed.
  </p>
  <h2>What we don't do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No accounts, OAuth, or login of any kind.</li>
    <li>No comments, reactions, or follows.</li>
    <li>No submission form — discovery is zero-touch by design.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="meta">
    Currently indexing {shown.length} post{shown.length === 1 ? "" : "s"} from
    {authors(posts).length} author{authors(posts).length === 1 ? "" : "s"}.
  </p>
</Base>
